TILE ENGINE RETRO — RESURRECTION PLAN (2026-07-26)

Goal: back from the graveyard, nice demo for Luis in a few weeks.

== 1. RESURRECTION (make it build and run again) ==

[x] Load bg0.gfx into bg[0] (was loading bg1.gfx twice)
[x] Fix hardcoded /home/daniel/... music path (load test.xm relative to cwd,
    same as the .gfx files)
[x] NULL-check every fopen; missing assets log an error instead of segfaulting
[x] Remove unused audiofile handle (fopen("airwolf2.mod") / fclose(NULL) crash)
[x] Root + core Makefiles work on modern macOS (arm64, .dylib); drop dead
    -arch i386/x86_64 universal flags; make clean uses rm -f
[x] libxmp optional behind HAVE_XMP (auto-detected via pkg-config, override
    with make HAVE_XMP=0/1); core builds silent without it
[x] Fix delete_fsp/delete_hsp underflow (OOB read/infinite loop when deleting
    the last sprite)
[x] add_player handles add_fsp failure instead of using 32 as a sprite id
[x] add_projectile increments projectile_count
[x] player.score uint16_t -> uint32_t (default hi-scores exceed 65535)
[x] Normalize diagonal speed (DIA_SPD 12 -> 8, ~= 12/sqrt(2))
[x] Delete vestigial libretro-example skeleton: x_coord/y_coord fake
    serialization, retro_load_game_special magic numbers

== 2. ENGINE CORRECTNESS & COMPLETENESS ==

[x] SoA it is: game2.h completed and wired in, game.h deleted
    (the uint8_t<256 infinite loop died with the port)
[x] OAM transforms, all of them: h-flip + rotate +/-90 via pre-computed
    tileset variants (memory), v-flip + double-size at render time (cpu);
    rotation+h_flip+v_flip composes to -90
[x] Collisions: AABB on the packed dimensions words (projectiles vs
    enemies, players vs enemies) — no wraparound handling yet
[x] Free lists replace the active_number high-water mark (O(1) alloc,
    double-free guard)
[x] Readme reconciled with code: 4bpp everywhere (hsp now 8 palettes x 16
    colors, dead 3bpp masks deleted), 512x512 layers kept, actual GFX byte
    format documented, real render order (BG1, BG0, SP0, SP1) documented
[x] Save states: versioned manifest of memcpy'd blocks (~15 KB), verified
    byte-identical on a serialize/restore/replay round trip

== 3. RENDERER ==

[ ] Per-tile-row span rendering instead of per-pixel div/mod tilemap lookups
[ ] Factor the 3x-duplicated BG1 sampling into one sample_bg() helper
[ ] Consume the 8-pixel uint32_t fetch without re-shifting per pixel
[ ] Clip sprites once per sprite (visible span), not per pixel
[ ] Dirty-row/dirty-tile tracking for mostly-static backgrounds
[ ] Fade in/out via palette darkening (64 multiplies, not 76800) — old TODO item
[x] Vertical flip, rotation (see OAM transforms above)

== 4. TOOLING (bmptogfx is too obtuse) ==

[ ] Manifest-driven conversion: one small config per asset pack replaces
    positional args, the 4x4-BMP palette heuristic, and .pal.clr sidecars
[ ] PNG input (stb_image) so assets come straight out of Aseprite
[ ] Reverse direction: gfx -> PNG dump for verification
[ ] Deduplicate identical tiles (and mirrored ones once flips exist)
[ ] Tiled .tmx -> tilemap blob converter (replace hand-poked test pattern)
[ ] Validate inputs, fail loudly: bit depth, color count, tile overflow,
    >16 inputs (currently silent stack smash)

== 5. STRUCTURE & LONGEVITY ==

[ ] Split headers into .h/.c so the engine links as a library
[ ] Pass state explicitly (gfx_context*) instead of globals
[ ] Tests for the pure parts: bit-pack accessors, GFX parser round-trip,
    average_colors
[ ] SDL2 or PNG-out harness: run the engine without RetroArch (kills the
    debug-by-commit loop of Feb 2018)
[ ] Events/timeline system: "at frame N spawn wave X" (events.h successor —
    Luis's old department)
[ ] Audio engine proper: audio_batch_cb, SFX mixing, sane sample rate
[ ] -Wall -Wextra clean, clang-format, README with build-and-run GIF

== DEMO TARGET (Readme "Roadmap to 0.1", the unfinished half) ==

[ ] Collisions
[ ] Sprites for ships, explosions and bullets
[ ] Audio for bullets and hits
[ ] One level and boss
